{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":640,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:2Chr.14","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"2 Chronicles","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"2 Chronicles 14","reference":"2 Chronicles 14","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"The piety of Asa, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-5.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"His policy, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"6-8.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"His victory over the Ethiopians, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"9-15.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":8,"text":"Quiet - There was no open war, but there were private hostilities between his and Baasha's subjects.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":9,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":10,"text":"The land had rest - Those have rest indeed, to whom God gives rest; peace indeed, to whom Christ gives peace.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":11,"text":"We find by experience, it is good to seek the Lord.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":12,"text":"While we pursue the world, we meet with nothing but vexation.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":13,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":14,"text":"Before us - In our power.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":15,"text":"9.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":16,"text":"Ethiopian - Or, the Arabian, as the Hebrew word Cush is commonly used: these being much nearer to Asa than the Ethiopians.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":17,"text":"11.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":18,"text":"Let not man prevail - If he prevails against us, he prevails, as it were, against thee; because thou art our God.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":19,"text":"And we rest on thee, and go forth in thy name, which thou hast encouraged us to do.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":20,"text":"12.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":21,"text":"Smote - With terror, and an unaccountable consternation.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":22,"text":"14.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":23,"text":"Smote the cities - because they had joined, with Zerah in this war.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":14}}